# Git line-ending & diff policy for Psiphon-3X-UI.
#
# WHY: On Windows dev hosts ``core.autocrlf=true`` converts LF ↔ CRLF on
# checkout/commit. That's fine for code (IDEs cope) BUT it means the SHA256
# of the working-tree copy of an artefact differs from the SHA256 of the
# git blob (which is LF-canonical). raw.githubusercontent.com serves the
# git blob, so the operator-facing ``sha256sum -c release-artifacts.sha256``
# verification must compute the same hash the operator sees after a fresh
# ``git clone`` — i.e. the LF-canonical hash, not the working-tree hash.
#
# Pinning ``eol=lf`` for the SHIPPED artefacts (install scripts, panel HTML,
# i18n JSON, manifest itself) keeps those hashes stable across hosts without
# retraining contributors' editors. Source Python/JS/etc. inherit git's
# default text handling.
#
# To re-normalise the working tree after editing this file:
#   git add --renormalize .
#   git commit -m "chore: enforce .gitattributes line-ending policy"

# ── Shipped operator-facing release artefacts (LF canonical) ──────────────
*.sh               text eol=lf
*.html             text eol=lf
*.css              text eol=lf
*.js               text eol=lf
*.json             text eol=lf
install.sh         text eol=lf
release-artifacts.sha256  text eol=lf
# Phase 24 Hotfix #3: the templated per-country tunnel unit
# (systemd/psiphon-tunnel@.service) is shipped to operators via the installer
# (installer/panel_install.sh copies it to /etc/systemd/system/) and is a
# tracked release artefact in release-artifacts.sha256. Pin it LF so the
# working-tree SHA matches the git-blob SHA served by raw.githubusercontent.com
# (otherwise operators running `sha256sum -c release-artifacts.sha256` after a
# fresh `git clone` would see a mismatch on hosts where core.autocrlf=true
# silently CRLF-converted the file on checkout).
*.service          text eol=lf
# Phase 25 Hotfix #10: psiphon-xray-applier.path (systemd path unit) is
# shipped + installed by panel_install.sh; pin LF so the working-tree SHA
# matches the git-blob SHA served by raw.githubusercontent.com.
*.path             text eol=lf

# Phase 25 Hotfix #10: the applier's bash driver + stdlib-only json merger
# are root-owned helpers installed to /usr/local/libexec/psiphon-3x-ui/.
# *.sh is already LF-pinned at the top of this block; the .py helper
# inherits the generic `*.py text` rule below which uses git's default
# text handling on Linux and is safe for the operator-side install copy.

# ── Python source (default text = LF on commit) ─────────────────────────
*.py               text

# ── Documentation ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.md               text eol=lf

# ── Binary assets (no line-ending conversion) ───────────────────────────
*.png              binary
*.jpg              binary
*.ico              binary
*.svg              text eol=lf
*.woff2            binary
